{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-205f5f9b-5119-4481-8997-de3a406e5b1b-11\nfc_7f728cc1-8f55-950e-ae41-54617066bb93_1","tool_call":{"grepToolCall":{"args":{"pattern":"notes|Acceptance|acceptance|Quality|start\\.sh|self-contained|node_id","path":"/root/.cursor/projects/work-ws-worktrees-app-qa-engineer-1/agent-tools/6b4d8ca6-ff2c-4043-ade8-2919af822c7e.txt","caseInsensitive":false,"multiline":false,"toolCallId":"call-205f5f9b-5119-4481-8997-de3a406e5b1b-11\nfc_7f728cc1-8f55-950e-ae41-54617066bb93_1","offset":0},"result":{"success":{"pattern":"notes|Acceptance|acceptance|Quality|start\\.sh|self-contained|node_id","path":"/root/.cursor/projects/work-ws-worktrees-app-qa-engineer-1/agent-tools/6b4d8ca6-ff2c-4043-ade8-2919af822c7e.txt","outputMode":"content","workspaceResults":{"/work/ws/worktrees/app/qa-engineer-1":{"content":{"matches":[{"file":"../../../../../root/.cursor/projects/work-ws-worktrees-app-qa-engineer-1/agent-tools/6b4d8ca6-ff2c-4043-ade8-2919af822c7e.txt","matches":[{"lineNumber":13,"content":"  \"description\": \"Build a self-contained Slack-like team chat at /app. start.sh stays foreground and keeps serving. Three HTTP nodes on 127.0.0.1:8000/8001/8002, IRC on :6667, browser UI at GET /. Local Redis pub/sub on :6379 with fan-out that survives Redis kill. Covers auth, profiles, workspaces, invitations, roles, channels, DMs, messages, threads, reactions, pins, files, search, groups, slash commands, mentions, read state, settings, SPA with pinned testids, WebSocket dense seq, and IRC bridging. No remote services, no Slack SDK, no Docker-in-Docker.\",","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":127,"content":"      \"title\": \"Bootstrap cluster: start.sh, 3 HTTP nodes, Redis, health\",","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":189,"content":"      \"title\": \"Verify: start.sh self-contained port topology\",","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":273,"content":"  \"title\": \"Bootstrap cluster: start.sh, 3 HTTP nodes, Redis, health\",","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":283,"content":"  \"design\": \"## Summary\\n\\nMARATHON-2 bootstraps the Huddle cluster runtime at `/app`: a foreground `start.sh` that launches local Redis on `127.0.0.1:6379` and three identical HTTP nodes on `127.0.0.1:8000/8001/8002`, keeps them alive under SIGKILL (HTTP respawn ≤60s; Redis respawn after kill), and exposes a stable `GET /api/health` contract returning `{status:\\\"ok\\\", node_id}` with `node_id` ∈ `{0,1,2}` matching ports. This is the foundation every later auth, messaging, WS, IRC, and SPA task assumes: process topology, port map, node identity, and local-only Redis.\\n\\n## Technical Approach\\n\\n### Decision\\n- **Process model:** One bash supervisor (`/app/start.sh`) stays in the foreground and owns child lifetimes. Children: one `redis-server` + three Node.js HTTP workers. The supervisor polls PIDs (≈1s cadence) and respawns any dead child without exiting.\\n- **HTTP runtime:** **Node.js** (v24 present in the environment) using the **stdlib `http` module only** for this task—no npm regis [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":286,"content":"  \"notes\": \"Implemented start.sh supervisor (Redis :6379 + nodes :8000/8001/8002 with ~1s respawn), server/index.js + health.js (GET /api/health → {status:ok, node_id} number, Redis-independent), package.json, redis.conf. Verified: unit tests, integration (health map, node SIGKILL respawn ≤60s, Redis SIGKILL with health still 200). No migration.\",","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":292,"content":"  \"description\": \"Implement /app/start.sh that stays in the foreground, launches Redis on 127.0.0.1:6379, and three HTTP nodes on :8000/:8001/:8002. Auto-respawn killed HTTP nodes within 60s and Redis after kill. GET /api/health on each node returns 200 {status:ok, node_id} with node_id 0/1/2 matching ports. Self-contained; no remote services or Docker-in-Docker.\",","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":305,"content":"      \"text\": \"CRITIC REVIEW attempt=1 commit=e2704f33e188e66eba9d4d4225e79b74f8cd9ea1 APPROVED — start.sh supervises Redis@127.0.0.1:6379 + nodes 8000/1/2 with ~1s respawn; GET /api/health returns {status:\\\"ok\\\", node_id} as JSON number with correct Content-Type and no Redis dependency; integration verified kill/respawn and health-during-Redis-outage.\",","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":372,"content":"    \"title\": \"Bootstrap cluster: start.sh, 3 HTTP nodes, Redis, health\",","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":382,"content":"    \"design\": \"## Summary\\n\\nMARATHON-2 bootstraps the Huddle cluster runtime at `/app`: a foreground `start.sh` that launches local Redis on `127.0.0.1:6379` and three identical HTTP nodes on `127.0.0.1:8000/8001/8002`, keeps them alive under SIGKILL (HTTP respawn ≤60s; Redis respawn after kill), and exposes a stable `GET /api/health` contract returning `{status:\\\"ok\\\", node_id}` with `node_id` ∈ `{0,1,2}` matching ports. This is the foundation every later auth, messaging, WS, IRC, and SPA task assumes: process topology, port map, node identity, and local-only Redis.\\n\\n## Technical Approach\\n\\n### Decision\\n- **Process model:** One bash supervisor (`/app/start.sh`) stays in the foreground and owns child lifetimes. Children: one `redis-server` + three Node.js HTTP workers. The supervisor polls PIDs (≈1s cadence) and respawns any dead child without exiting.\\n- **HTTP runtime:** **Node.js** (v24 present in the environment) using the **stdlib `http` module only** for this task—no npm reg [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":385,"content":"    \"notes\": \"Implemented start.sh supervisor (Redis :6379 + nodes :8000/8001/8002 with ~1s respawn), server/index.js + health.js (GET /api/health → {status:ok, node_id} number, Redis-independent), package.json, redis.conf. Verified: unit tests, integration (health map, node SIGKILL respawn ≤60s, Redis SIGKILL with health still 200). No migration.\",","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":405,"content":"    \"design\": \"## Summary\\n\\nMARATHON-3 implements cluster-wide authentication for Huddle: `POST /api/auth/register`, `POST /api/auth/login`, and `GET /api/auth/me`, plus the shared durable user/token store that all three HTTP nodes read and write. It establishes the `UserObj` identity shape, opaque bearer tokens (`Authorization: Bearer …`), password hashing, username slug validation, and a reusable auth middleware that every later authenticated route (workspaces, channels, WS, IRC `PASS`, SPA) will call. Without this seam, no other feature can attribute callers or survive a request to a different node.\\n\\n## Technical Approach\\n\\n### Decision\\n- **Runtime:** Stay on the MARATHON-2 stack: Node.js stdlib `http` router in `server/index.js`, no Express/Fastify required.\\n- **Durable shared store:** One **SQLite** database file at `/app/data/huddle.db`, opened by each HTTP worker via Node’s built-in **`node:sqlite` (`DatabaseSync`)**. Enable **WAL** + a non-zero `busy_timeout` so concurren [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":408,"content":"    \"notes\": \"FEEDBACK attempt=1: critic requested changes; see CRITIC comment\",","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]}],"totalLines":13,"totalMatchedLines":13,"clientTruncated":false,"ripgrepTruncated":false}}}}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-205f5f9b-5119-4481-8997-de3a406e5b1b-11\nfc_7f728cc1-8f55-950e-ae41-54617066bb93_1","startedAtMs":"1787428022523","completedAtMs":"1787428022868"},"model_call_id":"65561474-8f2f-4b68-b5c5-4654114fd2b7-3-ktke","session_id":"f08db716-6338-4173-81dd-7a306c86fe4a","timestamp_ms":1787428022890}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"started","call_id":"call-205f5f9b-5119-4481-8997-de3a406e5b1b-12\nfc_7f728cc1-8f55-950e-ae41-54617066bb93_2","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/work/ws/worktrees/app/qa-engineer-1/server/index.js"}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-205f5f9b-5119-4481-8997-de3a406e5b1b-12\nfc_7f728cc1-8f55-950e-ae41-54617066bb93_2","startedAtMs":"1787428022820"},"model_call_id":"65561474-8f2f-4b68-b5c5-4654114fd2b7-3-ktke","session_id":"f08db716-6338-4173-81dd-7a306c86fe4a","timestamp_ms":1787428023095}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-205f5f9b-5119-4481-8997-de3a406e5b1b-12\nfc_7f728cc1-8f55-950e-ae41-54617066bb93_2","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/work/ws/worktrees/app/qa-engineer-1/server/index.js"},"result":{"success":{"content":"'use strict';\n\nconst http = require('http');\nconst { sendHealth } = require('./health');\n\nfunction parseEnv() {\n  const rawId = process.env.NODE_ID;\n  const rawPort = process.env.PORT;\n\n  if (rawId === undefined || rawId === '') {\n    console.error('NODE_ID is required (0, 1, or 2)');\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n\n  const nodeId = Number(rawId);\n  if (!Number.isInteger(nodeId) || nodeId < 0 || nodeId > 2) {\n    console.error(`Invalid NODE_ID: ${rawId} (must be integer 0, 1, or 2)`);\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n\n  if (rawPort === undefined || rawPort === '') {\n    console.error('PORT is required');\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n\n  const port = Number(rawPort);\n  const expected = 8000 + nodeId;\n  if (!Number.isInteger(port) || port !== expected) {\n    console.error(`PORT must equal 8000+NODE_ID (${expected}), got: ${rawPort}`);\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n\n  return { nodeId, port };\n}\n\nconst { nodeId, port } = parseEnv();\n\nconst server = http.createServer((req, res) => {\n  let pathname = '/';\n  try {\n    pathname = new URL(req.url || '/', `http://127.0.0.1:${port}`).pathname;\n  } catch {\n    pathname = '/';\n  }\n\n  if (pathname === '/api/health') {\n    if (req.method === 'GET') {\n      sendHealth(res, nodeId);\n      return;\n    }\n    const body = JSON.stringify({ error: 'method_not_allowed' });\n    res.writeHead(405, {\n      'Content-Type': 'application/json; charset=utf-8',\n      'Content-Length': Buffer.byteLength(body),\n    });\n    res.end(body);\n    return;\n  }\n\n  const body = JSON.stringify({ error: 'not_found' });\n  res.writeHead(404, {\n    'Content-Type': 'application/json; charset=utf-8',\n    'Content-Length': Buffer.byteLength(body),\n  });\n  res.end(body);\n});\n\nserver.on('error', (err) => {\n  console.error(`[node-${nodeId}] Failed to bind 127.0.0.1:${port}: ${err.message}`);\n  process.exit(1);\n});\n\nserver.listen(port, '127.0.0.1', () => {\n  console.error(`[node-${nodeId}] listening on 127.0.0.1:${port}`);\n});\n","isEmpty":false,"exceededLimit":false,"totalLines":76,"fileSize":1934,"path":"/work/ws/worktrees/app/qa-engineer-1/server/index.js","readRange":{"startLine":1,"endLine":76},"relatedCursorRulePaths":[],"relatedCursorRules":[]}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-205f5f9b-5119-4481-8997-de3a406e5b1b-12\nfc_7f728cc1-8f55-950e-ae41-54617066bb93_2","startedAtMs":"1787428022820","completedAtMs":"1787428023119"},"model_call_id":"65561474-8f2f-4b68-b5c5-4654114fd2b7-3-ktke","session_id":"f08db716-6338-4173-81dd-7a306c86fe4a","timestamp_ms":1787428023143}
