vNull":true,"redirects":[{"operator":">","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/dev/null"},{"operator":">","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/dev/null"},{"operator":">","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/dev/null"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Show epic and related task details","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"2804cb91-d693-43d5-9a04-b7f3412a8025","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"result":{"success":{"command":"loom data show MARATHON-1 && echo '---' && loom data show MARATHON-24 --output json 2>/dev/null | head -c 5000; echo; loom data comments MARATHON-27 2>/dev/null; loom data show MARATHON-26 --output json 2>/dev/null | head -c 3000","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"ID:       MARATHON-1\nTitle:    Huddle: Slack-like team chat cluster\nStatus:   open\nPriority: 2\nType:     epic\nOwner:    marathon-harness\n\nDescription:\nBuild a self-contained Slack-like team chat at /app. start.sh stays foreground and keeps serving. Three HTTP nodes on 127.0.0.1:8000/8001/8002, IRC on :6667, browser UI at GET /. Local Redis pub/sub on :6379 with fan-out that survives Redis kill. Covers auth, profiles, workspaces, invitations, roles, channels, DMs, messages, threads, reactions, pins, files, search, groups, slash commands, mentions, read state, settings, SPA with pinned testids, WebSocket dense seq, and IRC bridging. No remote services, no Slack SDK, no Docker-in-Docker.\n---\n{\n  \"id\": \"MARATHON-24\",\n  \"title\": \"Verify: cluster bootstrap health and respawn\",\n  \"status\": \"closed\",\n  \"priority\": 2,\n  \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n  \"owner\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"labels\": [\n    \"qa\"\n  ],\n  \"source_repo\": \"app\",\n  \"parent\": \"MARATHON-1\",\n  \"has_design\": false,\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:41:32.029300129Z\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:46:41.266724208Z\",\n  \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:46:41.266724208Z\",\n  \"close_reason\": \"integrated into /app by harness gate (attempt=1)\",\n  \"description\": \"On integrated head e2704f3 (MARATHON-2), verify against the product specification: /app/start.sh stays foreground and serves three HTTP nodes on 127.0.0.1:8000/8001/8002 plus Redis on 127.0.0.1:6379; GET /api/health on each node returns 200 {\\\"status\\\":\\\"ok\\\",\\\"node_id\\\":N} with node_id 0/1/2 matching ports (JSON number); SIGKILL of one HTTP node restores that port's health within 60s without stopping the other two; SIGKILL of redis-server leaves health still 200 on all nodes and Redis is respawned by start.sh. No Docker or remote services.\",\n  \"comments\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": 7,\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-24\",\n      \"author\": \"qa-engineer-1\",\n      \"text\": \"IMPL-DONE attempt=1 commit=7077d7f36a70d3cf5969335e75c028fdaeb131f6\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:44:17.767607717Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": 8,\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-24\",\n      \"author\": \"marathon-harness\",\n      \"text\": \"CRITIC REVIEW attempt=1 commit=7077d7f36a70d3cf5969335e75c028fdaeb131f6 APPROVED — qa-cluster-bootstrap.sh covers MARATHON-2 AC1–AC9 (foreground supervisor, Redis PING, health JSON number map on :8000/1/2, HTTP SIGKILL respawn ≤60s with siblings up, Redis SIGKILL with health still 200 + respawn, local-only) plus non-GET edge; script run green (15/0).\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:46:41.081535981Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": 9,\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-24\",\n      \"author\": \"marathon-harness\",\n      \"text\": \"INTEGRATED attempt=1 app_before=e2704f33e188e66eba9d4d4225e79b74f8cd9ea1 app_after=7077d7f36a70d3cf5969335e75c028fdaeb131f6\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:46:41.245993488Z\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nThe 'loom data' subtree contains thin CLI commands that interact\nwith the configured loom issue backend. When --server or LOOM_SERVER_URL is\nset, commands talk to that loom server over HTTP. Without a server, issue\ncommands use the local backend selected by the workspace configuration and\ndaemon IPC environment.\n\nUse 'loom data' commands when:\n  • You want a backend-aware command surface for agents and scripts.\n  • You want to manage agents on a remote loom server.\n  • You are scripting against a hosted loom deployment.\n\nExamples:\n  loom data show <id> --server http://localhost:8080\n  loom data ready --limit 10\n  loom data list --server http://localhost:8080 -o json | jq '.[].id'\n  loom data monitor --server http://localhost:8080\n  loom data agent stop falcon --server http://localhost:8080\n\nRoot-level --server / --workspace are mirrored into LOOM_SERVER_URL /\nLOOM_WORKSPACE in PersistentPreRunE, so 'loom --server URL data show ID'\nand 'loom data show ID --server URL' resolve identically. The data\nsubcommand reads from env, not from its own flag.\n\nUsage:\n  loom data [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  agent       Control a single agent on the loom server (stop/start/restart/yield)\n  agents      List agents managed by the loom server daemon (HTTP)\n  blocked     List issues that are blocked by other open issues (HTTP)\n  claim       Atomically claim an issue\n  close       Close an issue (HTTP)\n  comment     Add a comment to an issue (HTTP)\n  create      Create an issue\n  list        List issues (HTTP)\n  monitor     Show monitor dashboard from a loom server (HTTP, single-shot)\n  ready       List issues that are ready to work on (HTTP)\n  show        Show a single issue by ID (HTTP)\n  update      Update issue fields\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help            help for data\n  -o, --output string   Output format: text|json (default \"text\")\n      --server string   Loom server base URL (or LOOM_SERVER_URL env var)\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --backend string      AI backend CLI to use (codex, claude, opencode). Env: LOOM_BACKEND\n      --log-format string   Log format (text|json) (default \"text\")\n      --log-output string   Log output destination (stderr|<filepath>) (default \"stderr\")\n      --workspace string    Workspace ID. Env: LOOM_WORKSPACE\n\nUse \"loom data [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n{\n  \"id\": \"MARATHON-26\",\n  \"title\": \"Verify: health node_id map on head 7077d7f\",\n  \"status\": \"review\",\n  \"priority\": 2,\n  \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n  \"owner\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"labels\": [\n    \"qa\"\n  ],\n  \"source_repo\": \"app\",\n  \"parent\": \"MARATHON-1\",\n  \"has_design\": false,\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:48:49.531504067Z\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:53:31.077485068Z\",\n  \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"description\": \"On integrated head 7077d7f (after MARATHON-24), verify against the product specification: with /app/start.sh running, GET /api/health on 127.0.0.1:8000, :8001, and :8002 each returns 200 with JSON status exactly \\\\\\\"ok\\\\\\\" and node_id JSON numbers 0, 1, and 2 respectively; health succeeds while Redis is down; the service remains self-contained with no remote dependencies.\",\n  \"comments\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": 17,\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-26\",\n      \"author\": \"qa-engineer-1\",\n      \"text\": \"IMPL-DONE attempt=1 commit=a4042b2864ed1e19a510697b25e4fc7d8148208f\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:53:31.03856251Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": 18,\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-26\",\n      \"author\": \"qa-engineer-1\",\n      \"text\": \"QA RESULTS: pass — qa-health-node-id.sh 11/0 (C1 map :8000→0/:8001→1/:8002→2 status=ok JSON numbers; inverted map rejected; health 200 while Redis down; self-contained no remote deps). defects filed: none\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:53:31.112183199Z\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","stderr":"time=2026-08-22T19:54:07.075Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:38569\n","executionTime":364,"interleavedOutput":"time=2026-08-22T19:54:07.075Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:38569\nID:       MARATHON-1\nTitle:    Huddle: Slack-like team chat cluster\nStatus:   open\nPriority: 2\nType:     epic\nOwner:    marathon-harness\n\nDescription:\nBuild a self-contained Slack-like team chat at /app. start.sh stays foreground and keeps serving. Three HTTP nodes on 127.0.0.1:8000/8001/8002, IRC on :6667, browser UI at GET /. Local Redis pub/sub on :6379 with fan-out that survives Redis kill. Covers auth, profiles, workspaces, invitations, roles, channels, DMs, messages, threads, reactions, pins, files, search, groups, slash commands, mentions, read state, settings, SPA with pinned testids, WebSocket dense seq, and IRC bridging. No remote services, no Slack SDK, no Docker-in-Docker.\n---\n{\n  \"id\": \"MARATHON-24\",\n  \"title\": \"Verify: cluster bootstrap health and respawn\",\n  \"status\": \"closed\",\n  \"priority\": 2,\n  \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n  \"owner\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"labels\": [\n    \"qa\"\n  ],\n  \"source_repo\": \"app\",\n  \"parent\": \"MARATHON-1\",\n  \"has_design\": false,\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:41:32.029300129Z\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:46:41.266724208Z\",\n  \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:46:41.266724208Z\",\n  \"close_reason\": \"integrated into /app by harness gate (attempt=1)\",\n  \"description\": \"On integrated head e2704f3 (MARATHON-2), verify against the product specification: /app/start.sh stays foreground and serves three HTTP nodes on 127.0.0.1:8000/8001/8002 plus Redis on 127.0.0.1:6379; GET /api/health on each node returns 200 {\\\"status\\\":\\\"ok\\\",\\\"node_id\\\":N} with node_id 0/1/2 matching ports (JSON number); SIGKILL of one HTTP node restores that port's health within 60s without stopping the other two; SIGKILL of redis-server leaves health still 200 on all nodes and Redis is respawned by start.sh. No Docker or remote services.\",\n  \"comments\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": 7,\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-24\",\n      \"author\": \"qa-engineer-1\",\n      \"text\": \"IMPL-DONE attempt=1 commit=7077d7f36a70d3cf5969335e75c028fdaeb131f6\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:44:17.767607717Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": 8,\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-24\",\n      \"author\": \"marathon-harness\",\n      \"text\": \"CRITIC REVIEW attempt=1 commit=7077d7f36a70d3cf5969335e75c028fdaeb131f6 APPROVED — qa-cluster-bootstrap.sh covers MARATHON-2 AC1–AC9 (foreground supervisor, Redis PING, health JSON number map on :8000/1/2, HTTP SIGKILL respawn ≤60s with siblings up, Redis SIGKILL with health still 200 + respawn, local-only) plus non-GET edge; script run green (15/0).\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:46:41.081535981Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": 9,\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-24\",\n      \"author\": \"marathon-harness\",\n      \"text\": \"INTEGRATED attempt=1 app_before=e2704f33e188e66eba9d4d4225e79b74f8cd9ea1 app_after=7077d7f36a70d3cf5969335e75c028fdaeb131f6\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:46:41.245993488Z\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nThe 'loom data' subtree contains thin CLI commands that interact\nwith the configured loom issue backend. When --server or LOOM_SERVER_URL is\nset, commands talk to that loom server over HTTP. Without a server, issue\ncommands use the local backend selected by the workspace configuration and\ndaemon IPC environment.\n\nUse 'loom data' commands when:\n  • You want a backend-aware command surface for agents and scripts.\n  • You want to manage agents on a remote loom server.\n  • You are scripting against a hosted loom deployment.\n\nExamples:\n  loom data show <id> --server http://localhost:8080\n  loom data ready --limit 10\n  loom data list --server http://localhost:8080 -o json | jq '.[].id'\n  loom data monitor --server http://localhost:8080\n  loom data agent stop falcon --server http://localhost:8080\n\nRoot-level --server / --workspace are mirrored into LOOM_SERVER_URL /\nLOOM_WORKSPACE in PersistentPreRunE, so 'loom --server URL data show ID'\nand 'loom data show ID --server URL' resolve identically. The data\nsubcommand reads from env, not from its own flag.\n\nUsage:\n  loom data [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  agent       Control a single agent on the loom server (stop/start/restart/yield)\n  agents      List agents managed by the loom server daemon (HTTP)\n  blocked     List issues that are blocked by other open issues (HTTP)\n  claim       Atomically claim an issue\n  close       Close an issue (HTTP)\n  comment     Add a comment to an issue (HTTP)\n  create      Create an issue\n  list        List issues (HTTP)\n  monitor     Show monitor dashboard from a loom server (HTTP, single-shot)\n  ready       List issues that are ready to work on (HTTP)\n  show        Show a single issue by ID (HTTP)\n  update      Update issue fields\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help            help for data\n  -o, --output string   Output format: text|json (default \"text\")\n      --server string   Loom server base URL (or LOOM_SERVER_URL env var)\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --backend string      AI backend CLI to use (codex, claude, opencode). Env: LOOM_BACKEND\n      --log-format string   Log format (text|json) (default \"text\")\n      --log-output string   Log output destination (stderr|<filepath>) (default \"stderr\")\n      --workspace string    Workspace ID. Env: LOOM_WORKSPACE\n\nUse \"loom data [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n{\n  \"id\": \"MARATHON-26\",\n  \"title\": \"Verify: health node_id map on head 7077d7f\",\n  \"status\": \"review\",\n  \"priority\": 2,\n  \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n  \"owner\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"labels\": [\n    \"qa\"\n  ],\n  \"source_repo\": \"app\",\n  \"parent\": \"MARATHON-1\",\n  \"has_design\": false,\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:48:49.531504067Z\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:53:31.077485068Z\",\n  \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"description\": \"On integrated head 7077d7f (after MARATHON-24), verify against the product specification: with /app/start.sh running, GET /api/health on 127.0.0.1:8000, :8001, and :8002 each returns 200 with JSON status exactly \\\\\\\"ok\\\\\\\" and node_id JSON numbers 0, 1, and 2 respectively; health succeeds while Redis is down; the service remains self-contained with no remote dependencies.\",\n  \"comments\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": 17,\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-26\",\n      \"author\": \"qa-engineer-1\",\n      \"text\": \"IMPL-DONE attempt=1 commit=a4042b2864ed1e19a510697b25e4fc7d8148208f\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:53:31.03856251Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": 18,\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-26\",\n      \"author\": \"qa-engineer-1\",\n      \"text\": \"QA RESULTS: pass — qa-health-node-id.sh 11/0 (C1 map :8000→0/:8001→1/:8002→2 status=ok JSON numbers; inverted map rejected; health 200 while Redis down; self-contained no remote deps). defects filed: none\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:53:31.112183199Z\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","localExecutionTimeMs":290},"isBackground":false},"description":"Show epic and related task details"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-da774483-59e1-4a15-8719-10c86b3642f7-2\nfc_614f277d-0390-963a-a2f1-52bc9a05e55e_0","startedAtMs":"1787428446924","completedAtMs":"1787428447291"},"model_call_id":"61595985-413d-43b0-aa35-71c44ed4f0ab-1-uwd6","session_id":"2804cb91-d693-43d5-9a04-b7f3412a8025","timestamp_ms":1787428447320}
